statement:
For n, k ∈ ℕ there are λ₀ > 0 and C₉ > 0, depending only on n and k (they are chosen after n, k, as in the Lean quantifier order ∀ (n k : ℕ), ∃ lam₀ C₉), with the following property. Let μ be a measure on ℝ^{n+k}, τ a map into linear subspaces (p_x := p_{τ(x)}, p_x^⊥u := u − p_x u), T₀ a subspace (P := p_{T₀}, Qu := u − Pu), F ⊆ ℝ^{n+k}, ξ ∈ spt μ, σ₀ > 0, κ ≥ 0 with κσ₀ ≤ 1 and 0 ≤ λ ≤ λ₀. Assume:
(F) |Q(x − x')| ≤ λ|x − x'| for all x, x' ∈ F;
(Da) μ(B_t(y)) ≤ 2ω_n tⁿ for y ∈ B_{σ₀/2}(ξ) and t ∈ (0, 5σ₀/8];
(Db) ω_n tⁿ ≤ 2μ(B_t(y)) for y ∈ spt μ ∩ B_{σ₀/2}(ξ) and t ∈ (0, σ₀/8];
(M2) e^{−κt}t^{−n}μ(B_t(y)) ≤ e^{−κs}s^{−n}μ(B_s(y)) + ∫_{B_t(y)∖B_s(y)} |p_x^⊥(x − y)|²|x − y|^{−n−2} dμ for y ∈ B_{σ₀/4}(ξ) and 0 < s < t ≤ 3σ₀/8.
Then for every η ∈ (F ∖ spt μ) ∩ B_{σ₀/4}(ξ) there are s > 0 and y ∈ spt μ with 2s ≤ |η − ξ|, |y − η| = 2s and sⁿ ≤ C₉[μ(B_{3s}(η) ∖ F) + ∫_{B_{3s}(η)} |p_x − P|² dμ].
Conventions: closed balls; extended-real inequalities with ENNReal.ofReal; lower Lebesgue integrals; |A|² is the Hilbert–Schmidt sum over EuclideanSpace.single i 1; ω_n = unitBallVolume n.
